00:36:12.030 --> 00:36:12.530
OK.

00:36:12.530 --> 00:36:14.820
Let's just double check.

00:36:14.820 --> 00:36:18.030
And we get-- so that's
going to play that out

00:36:18.030 --> 00:36:19.560
into my Kubernetes cluster.

00:36:19.560 --> 00:36:21.780
Exactly the same
if I'm a developer

00:36:21.780 --> 00:36:25.183
and I have an [INAUDIBLE]
looking after my GKE cluster.

00:36:25.183 --> 00:36:26.850
I don't need to worry
about all of that.

00:36:26.850 --> 00:36:28.420
It's a serverless experience.

00:36:28.420 --> 00:36:30.490
STEWART REICHLING: Yeah,
that's a good point.

00:36:30.490 --> 00:36:34.110
Cloud Run on GKE, well, you
have to have a GKE cluster.

00:36:34.110 --> 00:36:38.652
It's not as managed as the
Cloud Run experience is.

00:36:38.652 --> 00:36:40.110
If you already have
a cluster, It's

00:36:40.110 --> 00:36:42.717
a great way to actually get
started and get as much as you

00:36:42.717 --> 00:36:43.800
can out of your functions.

00:36:43.800 --> 00:36:46.920
If you don't have a cluster yet,
the easiest way to try to stuff

00:36:46.920 --> 00:36:49.815
out is to just go for Cloud Run,
because that's fully managed.

00:36:49.815 --> 00:36:50.690
JUSTIN GRAYSTON: Yep.

00:36:50.690 --> 00:36:51.660
OK.

00:36:51.660 --> 00:36:52.673
So let's just recap.

00:36:52.673 --> 00:36:54.590
We've deployed to three
different environments

00:36:54.590 --> 00:36:56.380
with exactly the same function.

00:36:56.380 --> 00:36:58.850
The only difference was
the environment variables.

00:36:58.850 --> 00:37:00.950
And we've gone to Cloud
Functions, Cloud Run--

00:37:00.950 --> 00:37:03.450
STEWART REICHLING: Well, you
wrote a little Docker file too.

00:37:03.450 --> 00:37:03.900
JUSTIN GRAYSTON: Yeah, I did.

00:37:03.900 --> 00:37:06.350
STEWART REICHLING: But yeah,
it's the same function code.

00:37:06.350 --> 00:37:07.980
JUSTIN GRAYSTON: We didn't
have to change the actual code

00:37:07.980 --> 00:37:08.220
at all.

00:37:08.220 --> 00:37:08.840
STEWART REICHLING: Exactly.

00:37:08.840 --> 00:37:09.210
JUSTIN GRAYSTON: OK.

00:37:09.210 --> 00:37:11.790
So hopefully, if the domain
gods are playing nicely,

00:37:11.790 --> 00:37:13.903
we should say hello
from GCF and US West.

00:37:13.903 --> 00:37:14.820
STEWART REICHLING: OK.

00:37:14.820 --> 00:37:17.525
You got a nice HTTPS URL
that you can invoke there.

00:37:17.525 --> 00:37:19.400
JUSTIN GRAYSTON: And
then we go to Cloud Run,

00:37:19.400 --> 00:37:21.960
and we head across
